        476.78
      ],
      "text": "7"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        131.94,
        461.49,
        232.13,
        476.78
      ],
      "text": "Fast sorting"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        486.42,
        358.76,
        502.04
      ],
      "text": "Theorem 2. For any a ≥2 and 2a/4 ≤m ≤2a/2,"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        223.07,
        512.22,
        323.48,
        529.46
      ],
      "text": "Pm(a) ≥2a+1/2 −O"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        325.8,
        515.96,
        331.28,
        523.61
      ],
      "text": "\u0000"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        331.28,
        512.22,
        374.3,
        528.44
      ],
      "text": "a−γ · 2a\u0001"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        376.3,
        517.83,
        379.55,
        528.44
      ],
      "text": ","
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        478.92,
        517.83,
        499.74,
        528.44
      ],
      "text": "(44)"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        542.29,
        285.9,
        554.84
      ],
      "text": "where γ is small enough, say, γ = 1"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        281.67,
        544.23,
        290.68,
        558.19
      ],
      "text": "5."
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        567.64,
        499.74,
        578.26
      ],
      "text": "Proof. We will apply Lemma 2 to the result of Lemma 4. The values of all"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        580.51,
        499.74,
        592.7
      ],
      "text": "parameters are borrowed from Lemma 4. We have v ∈T(σ[s]) and u ∈T ε(σ[s])"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        595.86,
        499.73,
        607.15
      ],
      "text": "for the system of restrictions σ[s] of depth h = 2s+3 and width w ≤s+4. Note"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        606.64,
        477.35,
        623.39
      ],
      "text": "that ui < 2yi−1/2 < π(yi), see (16). We also have ϵ < 1−λ < R = ||v−u|| <"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        480.67,
        600.42,
        490.63,
        611.7
      ],
      "text": "√"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        490.63,
        610.98,
        499.74,
        621.59
      ],
      "text": "2."
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        120.44,
        625.42,
        499.73,
        636.04
      ],
      "text": "For a < 100, the inequality (44) holds with suﬃciently large values of the"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        639.2,
        499.73,
        650.49
      ],
      "text": "constant hidden behind the symbol “O”. Thus, we may assume a ≥100. Set"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        654.32,
        141.47,
        664.93
      ],
      "text": "ϕ = log"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        143.62,
        647.4,
        162.44,
        660.1
      ],
      "text": "\u0000 mε"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        150.29,
        660.32,
        162.68,
        668.28
      ],
      "text": "4a2"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        164.37,
        652.45,
        169.85,
        660.1
      ],
      "text": "\u0001"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        173.81,
        652.74,
        499.73,
        664.93
      ],
      "text": "and s = ⌈2γ log a⌉. If γ ≤1/4, then mε ≥2a/4/(50 · a2γ) ≥4a2,"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        668.76,
        471.65,
        679.38
      ],
      "text": "hence, ϕ > 0. The condition (17) in Lemma 2 is automatically satisﬁed."
    }
