    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        303.73,
        499.23,
        316.8
      ],
      "text": "for n0 < k < n/2 −m, and at most log(2k −1) + O(1) comparisons for k ≤n0"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        318.17,
        499.74,
        329.46
      ],
      "text": "and k ≥n/2 −m. So, the excess number of comparisons with respect to (45)"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        333.29,
        208.04,
        343.9
      ],
      "text": "may be estimated as"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        201.33,
        360.74,
        279.44,
        373.15
      ],
      "text": "O(n0 + m) + O"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        281.76,
        355.29,
        288.9,
        362.94
      ],
      "text": "\u0010"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        288.9,
        355.59,
        388.9,
        372.37
      ],
      "text": "(n/2 −n0) log−1/5 n"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        388.91,
        355.29,
        396.05,
        362.94
      ],
      "text": "\u0011"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        398.04,
        360.74,
        401.29,
        371.35
      ],
      "text": "."
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        102.88,
        388.19,
        297.82,
        398.8
      ],
      "text": "Finally, we obtain a recurrent relation"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        121.87,
        414.97,
        406.04,
        426.26
      ],
      "text": "S(n) ≤n/2 + S(n/2) + log(n!) −log((n/2)!) −n/2 + O"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        408.36,
        410.19,
        415.5,
        417.84
      ],
      "text": "\u0010"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        415.5,
        410.49,
        468.36,
